{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786838726330936557,"compiled_state":{"alias":"peach-chemic-hairstreak","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"59dfc66046d027701562f7e44711110632efc540e83408b5c6531406fa714e48","event_uuid":"26e6a82f-6546-437c-af87-981d995c97f7","position":{"commit_sha":"d7ba8ba0411e336bd205ec9a22e1a2471fe782cd","position":"1786830307260419001-26e6a82f-6546-437c-af87-981d995c97f7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"667bec1bcfb6444bfe6613f6789219be0d6fd054be68a7da4e9ca505cfaeef1b","event_uuid":"a5dfa318-3d68-434e-b357-24806810b3dd","position":{"commit_sha":"13cb06c5386a680b1d4466c057775ba868bd9c50","position":"1786830319600129001-a5dfa318-3d68-434e-b357-24806810b3dd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8c24a8ba1a1d158d23cefe0c7da96c245501a5ce48d874c7ddfa38d9555d6cb7","event_uuid":"cdb38a1e-5f86-4278-9681-ffb3475473b6","position":{"commit_sha":"6e2e316251de5afa625d4759eabd9c3a07ff0072","position":"1786830332061483001-cdb38a1e-5f86-4278-9681-ffb3475473b6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786830307260419001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a5dfa318-3d68-434e-b357-24806810b3dd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4dd2-4217-318a-4613"},{"link_uuid":"cdb38a1e-5f86-4278-9681-ffb3475473b6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8274-6714-32b6-48be"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nObserved 2026-08-15 while cutting the 0.12.0 release (ticket grassgreen-unfearful-quoll): `rebar review-plan` failed with `LLMConfigError: a bedrock model/provider is configured but no AWS region could be resolved`, returning an unsigned INDETERMINATE and no LLM pass. The overlap step failed the same way (WARNING rebar.llm.overlap.wire: store-wide overlap step failed).\n\nReproduction environment (this checkout, a fresh non-login agent shell):\n- Env: only `AWS_PROFILE=frontier` exported — no `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION`, no `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`, no `AWS_REGION`.\n- `~/.aws/config`: `[profile frontier]` has NO `region` key (login_session only); `[default]` has `region = us-east-1` but is shadowed by AWS_PROFILE=frontier; `[profile frontier-bedrock]` carries `region = us-west-2` + a credential_process chaining to frontier, but is not the active profile.\n- Result: every resolution rung in the documented order (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION > AWS_DEFAULT_REGION > AWS_REGION > boto3 profile resolution) comes up empty and the provider raises.\n\nPrior art: closed bug saintly-letterhigh-yaffle (8274-6714-32b6-48be) added AWS_REGION to the env-var resolution order (the error message now lists it). That fix works but did not close THIS gap: env-var resolution cannot help a shell that exports none of the vars, and the active profile carries no region.\n\nRoot cause (residual): the repo config half is missing. `rebar.toml`'s `[llm]` table pins the Bedrock model IDs (region-scoped `us.` inference profiles, single-sourced from .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml) but does NOT set `bedrock_region_name`, even though the knob exists (src/rebar/llm/config.py:476,599-600 — `_llm_str(table, cli, \"REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION\", \"bedrock_region_name\", None)`). The checkout therefore knows exactly which region its pinned `us.*` profiles live in, yet makes every operator/agent shell rediscover it via ambient env — fresh agent shells (Copilot/Codex tool shells do not inherit login-shell exports) fail closed on every gated operation.\n\n## Approach\nSet `bedrock_region_name` in rebar.toml's `[llm]` table to the region the pinned `us.*` inference profiles are served from (us-west-2, matching the frontier-bedrock profile), so the checkout is self-sufficient: any shell with working AWS credentials runs the gates without per-command region injection. Env vars keep precedence (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION overrides the table value) so nothing regresses for operators who pin a different region. Consider recording in docs/config.md that a repo that pins region-scoped Bedrock inference profiles should pin the region beside them.\n\n## File impact\n- rebar.toml — set bedrock_region_name in [llm]\n- docs/config.md — note pairing region-scoped model pins with a pinned region (if guidance is missing)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] rebar.toml's [llm] table sets bedrock_region_name to the region matching the pinned us.* inference profiles.\n- [ ] In a shell exporting only AWS_PROFILE=frontier (no REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION, or AWS_REGION), `rebar review-plan <id> --status` and an LLM-bearing gate run resolve a region and do not raise LLMConfigError.\n- [ ] REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION env var still overrides the rebar.toml value (covered by an existing or new unit test).\n- [ ] The verdict's provider provenance records the region and its source as repo-config.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","8274-6714-32b6-48be"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"adb6-4762-90f6-4e30","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gated LLM ops fail closed in fresh shells: rebar.toml pins region-scoped Bedrock models but not bedrock_region_name","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["26e6a82f-6546-437c-af87-981d995c97f7","a5dfa318-3d68-434e-b357-24806810b3dd","cdb38a1e-5f86-4278-9681-ffb3475473b6"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786838726330936557,"uuid":"6d437e0a-8548-420d-91c3-2f16f25ff102"}